      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-d/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The tangent gradient is cos2(π/4)/(2 tan(π/4) + 1) = (1/2)/(2 + 1) = 1 2/3 . [A1] = 1/6 The normal has gradient −6 and equation y −π/4 = −6(x −3), [M1] giving y −π/4 = −6x + 18 and 4y −π = −24x + 72, so 4y + 24x = π + 72 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
